  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Every failure the gateway can produce maps to one of six statuses, and all of that mapping lives in a single exception handler. 400 means the request was invalid and we tell the merchant which field. 404 means unknown id. 409 is the idempotency conflict. 502 means the bank refused our request; 503 means we genuinely cannot know the result. 500 is the last-resort catch. Because this mapping exists in one place, the documentation, the tests, and the clients all see the same contract.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
